From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] gdm: keep the focus off the poster's hidden user list

The screen shield calls LoginDialog.activate() each time the greeter's
shield comes up, including on every idle blank, and activate() focuses
the user list. The poster (0227) keeps that list hidden, so its items are
never mapped and UserList._moveFocusToItems() can never move the focus to
one. It then retries before the next redraw, and each retry asks for that
redraw: the greeter drew a frame every refresh with the screen off. On a
Pixel 8 Pro the Shell woke about 180 times a second, used about 9 % of a
core and kept the memory bus at its top clock, as long as the greeter sat
blanked. Typed keys also went to the hidden list.

activate() now focuses the user list only when it is shown. The focus
stays with the visible prompt.

--- a/js/gdm/loginDialog.js
+++ b/js/gdm/loginDialog.js
@@ -1567,7 +1567,12 @@
     }
 
     activate() {
-        this._userList.grab_key_focus();
+        // The poster keeps the user list hidden. Its items are never mapped,
+        // so a focused UserList would retry focusing one before every redraw
+        // and keep the Shell drawing frames with the screen off, and typed
+        // keys would go nowhere. Leave the focus with the visible prompt.
+        if (this._userSelectionBox.visible)
+            this._userList.grab_key_focus();
         this.show();
     }
 
